+{"created_at": "2026-06-29T21:15:28.640711+00:00", "ocr_backend": "sglang", "ocr_endpoint_version": "modal-sglang-unlimited-ocr-v1", "ocr_model": "Unlimited-OCR", "ocr_model_version": "Unlimited-OCR", "ocr_text": "<PAGE><|det|>table [84, 58, 896, 145]<|/det|><table><tr><td>M-3</td><td colspan=\"3\">Vault Activation Possible During Bunker Mode, Enabling Bad Debt Attacks</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Medium</td><td>Status</td><td>Acknowledged</td></tr></table>\n<|det|>title [81, 166, 186, 180]<|/det|>Description\n<|det|>text [80, 183, 905, 336]<|/det|>Even while Lido v2 is in bunker mode, it is still possible to activate vaults and make deposits into them. While this does not directly affect the share rate, it opens up the possibility for an attack scenario where a malicious Node Operator intentionally increases bad debt through the malicious operation as a validator, which causes slashing penalties. This can worsen the protocol's state during bunker mode and potentially prolong the period in which Lido v2 remains in this critical state as the bad debt value increase is uncapped. The root cause is that the VaultHub contract's pause mechanism is independent from the main protocol's bunker mode, so vault operations are not automatically restricted when the protocol is in bunker mode.\n<|det|>text [80, 339, 898, 388]<|/det|>The issue is classified as Medium severity because it allows a malicious Node Operator worsen the bunker mode state and allows staking vaults to perform normally, while the Lido v2 protocol experiences the restrictions related to the bunker mode.\n<|det|>title [81, 409, 212, 421]<|/det|>Recommendation\n<|det|>text [80, 425, 915, 493]<|/det|>We recommend adding explicit checks for bunker mode status in the VaultHub contract, especially in functions that allow vault activation or deposits. The pause logic of VaultHub should be synchronized with the main protocol's bunker mode to prevent vault operations that could worsen protocol health during critical periods.\n<|det|>title [81, 514, 232, 527]<|/det|>Client's Commentary:\n<|det|>text [81, 530, 228, 544]<|/det|>Client: Need example\n<|det|>text [80, 548, 875, 613]<|/det|>Mixbytes: The risk of increasing the bad debt is very low since it is not that easy to cause slashing in the CS that would cause bad debt, but there is an invariant that there cannot be new deposits to validators during the bunker mode (this invariant exists in Lido v2) which is better to hold, since bunker mode means some abnormality in CS and it is better to resolve it before setting up new validators.\n<|det|>text [80, 617, 913, 666]<|/det|>Client: For the initial stage, when the amount of TVL in stVaults is limited, the proposed limitation looks to be the overkill, but the bunker mode should be improved to be able to scale up the stVaults somewhere further, so this recommendation implementation is postponed to the next release.\n<|det|>footer [81, 949, 248, 972]<|/det|>MixBytes()\n<|det|>page_number [880, 951, 916, 970]<|/det|>18\n", "page_image_sha256": "da2886fa0ec0420ba6b417837005cd023c9ba09552f3219df996f2cbfca8138c", "page_number": 19, "pdf_id": "pdf_003436_1e68fc3994b5", "raw_record": {"code_blocks": [], "confidence": null, "created_at": "2026-06-29T21:15:28.640711+00:00", "layout_blocks": [], "ocr_backend": "sglang", "ocr_endpoint_version": "modal-sglang-unlimited-ocr-v1", "ocr_model": "Unlimited-OCR", "ocr_model_version": "Unlimited-OCR", "ocr_settings": {"dpi": 300, "image_mode": "base", "mode": "pages", "ngram_size": 35, "ngram_window": 1024, "prompt": "Multi page parsing."}, "ocr_text": "<PAGE><|det|>table [84, 58, 896, 145]<|/det|><table><tr><td>M-3</td><td colspan=\"3\">Vault Activation Possible During Bunker Mode, Enabling Bad Debt Attacks</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Medium</td><td>Status</td><td>Acknowledged</td></tr></table>\n<|det|>title [81, 166, 186, 180]<|/det|>Description\n<|det|>text [80, 183, 905, 336]<|/det|>Even while Lido v2 is in bunker mode, it is still possible to activate vaults and make deposits into them. While this does not directly affect the share rate, it opens up the possibility for an attack scenario where a malicious Node Operator intentionally increases bad debt through the malicious operation as a validator, which causes slashing penalties. This can worsen the protocol's state during bunker mode and potentially prolong the period in which Lido v2 remains in this critical state as the bad debt value increase is uncapped. The root cause is that the VaultHub contract's pause mechanism is independent from the main protocol's bunker mode, so vault operations are not automatically restricted when the protocol is in bunker mode.\n<|det|>text [80, 339, 898, 388]<|/det|>The issue is classified as Medium severity because it allows a malicious Node Operator worsen the bunker mode state and allows staking vaults to perform normally, while the Lido v2 protocol experiences the restrictions related to the bunker mode.\n<|det|>title [81, 409, 212, 421]<|/det|>Recommendation\n<|det|>text [80, 425, 915, 493]<|/det|>We recommend adding explicit checks for bunker mode status in the VaultHub contract, especially in functions that allow vault activation or deposits. The pause logic of VaultHub should be synchronized with the main protocol's bunker mode to prevent vault operations that could worsen protocol health during critical periods.\n<|det|>title [81, 514, 232, 527]<|/det|>Client's Commentary:\n<|det|>text [81, 530, 228, 544]<|/det|>Client: Need example\n<|det|>text [80, 548, 875, 613]<|/det|>Mixbytes: The risk of increasing the bad debt is very low since it is not that easy to cause slashing in the CS that would cause bad debt, but there is an invariant that there cannot be new deposits to validators during the bunker mode (this invariant exists in Lido v2) which is better to hold, since bunker mode means some abnormality in CS and it is better to resolve it before setting up new validators.\n<|det|>text [80, 617, 913, 666]<|/det|>Client: For the initial stage, when the amount of TVL in stVaults is limited, the proposed limitation looks to be the overkill, but the bunker mode should be improved to be able to scale up the stVaults somewhere further, so this recommendation implementation is postponed to the next release.\n<|det|>footer [81, 949, 248, 972]<|/det|>MixBytes()\n<|det|>page_number [880, 951, 916, 970]<|/det|>18\n", "page_image_sha256": "da2886fa0ec0420ba6b417837005cd023c9ba09552f3219df996f2cbfca8138c", "page_number": 19, "pdf_id": "pdf_003436_1e68fc3994b5", "raw_response_ref": "chunk_0007/other_audit_repo_pdfs/pdf_003436_1e68fc3994b5_Lido_v3_Security_Audit_Report/pages_0017_0020.raw.json", "source_abs_path": "/home/experiments_base/smart-contract-data/crawlers/output/repos/audit_repos/audits_public/Lido/Lido v3/Lido v3 Security Audit Report.pdf", "source_bucket": "other_audit_repo_pdfs", "source_filename": "Lido v3 Security Audit Report.pdf", "source_page_count": 35, "source_pdf_sha256": "394412f5537fe8936dad4362cad9a71bf8d37c4bf7e759bdd2d021e4f98cbcda", "source_rel_path": "audits_public/Lido/Lido v3/Lido v3 Security Audit Report.pdf", "tables": [], "throughput": {"output_units": "tokens", "output_units_per_second": 438.0}, "timing_ms": {"decode": 1500, "sglang_total": 1691, "ttft": 191}, "usage": {"completion_token_source": "openai_usage", "completion_tokens": 657, "prompt_tokens": 278, "prompt_tokens_details": null, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "total_tokens": 935}, "warnings": []}, "raw_response_ref": "chunk_0007/other_audit_repo_pdfs/pdf_003436_1e68fc3994b5_Lido_v3_Security_Audit_Report/pages_0017_0020.raw.json", "schema_version": "evmbench_task_creation.ocr_page.v1", "source_bucket": "other_audit_repo_pdfs", "source_filename": "Lido v3 Security Audit Report.pdf", "source_page_count": 35, "source_pdf_sha256": "394412f5537fe8936dad4362cad9a71bf8d37c4bf7e759bdd2d021e4f98cbcda", "source_rel_path": "audits_public/Lido/Lido v3/Lido v3 Security Audit Report.pdf", "text_length": 